  "question": {
    "text": "The length of a given cylindrical wire is increased by $100 \\%$. Due to the consequent decrease in diameter the change in the resistance of the wire will be"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$200 \\%$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$100 \\%$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$50 \\%$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$300 \\%$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{L}_1=2 \\mathrm{l}$ or $\\left(\\pi \\mathrm{r}^2 \\mathrm{l}\\right)=\\left(\\pi \\mathrm{r}_2^2\\right)(2 \\mathrm{l})$\n$\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{r}_2=\\frac{\\mathrm{r}}{\\sqrt{2}}$$;$               $\\mathrm{R}=\\rho \\frac{1}{\\pi^2}$\n$\\mathrm{R}_{\\text {new }}=(\\rho) \\frac{21}{(\\pi)(\\mathrm{r} / \\sqrt{2})^2}=\\frac{(\\rho) 4 \\mathrm{l}}{(\\pi) \\mathrm{r}^2}=4 \\times \\mathrm{R}$\n$\\therefore \\Delta \\mathrm{R}=4 \\mathrm{R}-\\mathrm{R}=3 \\mathrm{R}$\n$\\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{R}}{\\mathrm{R}} \\%=\\frac{3 \\mathrm{R}}{\\mathrm{R}} \\times 100=300 \\%$"
  }
